# id  tag  kind  t_s  alt_km  L_si_W  flag  note
1 - first_light 1.4400 91.398 2.7044e+08 info  L_si first exceeds 1e-6 of its peak. This is just a visibility threshold; the real value depends on your sensor floor and on where the simulation starts (zstart).
2 A ablation_onset 2.5020 85.096 8.2342e+08 stylized  Net heating flux first exceeds radiative loss at T_ablate = 2300 K, so ablation switches on (a kink in the slope). Real onset is gradual over a few km. BELOW this point the model's light is drag work only (no ablated material): treat light above ~85 km as low-confidence. Loosely like the end of Phase 1 / start of Phase 2 in [R22], but the model has no spin, volatile (Na/K) emission or melt physics.
3 Y first_yield 10.2930 40.329 1.0954e+12 physical  Loading rho v^2 reaches S0 = 1.4 MPa. The body starts to flatten (pancake): area, drag and heating all grow, so the light rises faster. Analogue of the onset of fragmentation (Phase 5 / H_f in [R22]).
4 F flare 10.4920 39.220 1.9747e+12 stylized  Light rises x3.2 in 0.42 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated with: yield gen 0 at 40.3 km (100% of m0). Dust groups supply 0% of the rise and 0% of the light at the end of the flare. A real fragmentation flare (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come from the model's deterministic cascade.
5 B first_breakup 11.0970 35.864 9.4860e+12 stylized  Spread factor reached f_split = 2: the body breaks into 4 children plus 20 % of its mass as dust. The dust has a large area-to-mass ratio, decelerates and ablates within a fraction of a second, which makes a sharp flare. The instantaneous release is a model simplification. Light grew x8.7 between first yield and this breakup (pancake spreading).
6 P peak 11.1000 35.847 2.6997e+14 physical  Maximum light. It sits ~+7.1 km from the peak of energy deposition (28.8 km) because the luminous efficiency tau(v) falls as the fragments slow (mass-weighted speed here 19.1 km/s).
7 F flare 11.1017 35.838 2.6749e+14 stylized  Light rises x24.5 in 0.09 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated with: split gen 0 at 35.8 km (99% of m0); yield gen 1 at 35.8 km (38% of m0); yield gen 1 at 35.8 km (19% of m0). Dust groups supply 100% of the rise and 96% of the light at the end of the flare (the model releases dust all at once, so a dust-dominated first flare is by construction). A real fragmentation flare (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come from the model's deterministic cascade.
8 D rolloff 11.3160 34.737 9.8644e+13 physical  Light has fallen to 1/e of the peak 0.22 s after it. Cause: the kinetic energy is being used up (speed 98% of v0, 90% of the mass still in flight) and tau(v) drops with speed. Analogue of Phase 7 (decline until dark flight) in [R22].
9 F flare 11.6349 33.001 1.2398e+14 stylized  Light rises x1.8 in 0.09 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated with: split gen 1 at 32.9 km (18% of m0); yield gen 2 at 32.9 km (7% of m0); split gen 1 at 32.5 km (12% of m0). Dust groups supply 87% of the rise and 64% of the light at the end of the flare. A real fragmentation flare (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come from the model's deterministic cascade.
10 F flare 11.8003 32.108 1.2345e+14 stylized  Light rises x1.6 in 0.13 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated with: split gen 1 at 32.5 km (12% of m0); yield gen 2 at 32.2 km (5% of m0); split gen 1 at 32.2 km (9% of m0) +5 more. Dust groups supply 93% of the rise and 77% of the light at the end of the flare (the model releases dust all at once, so a dust-dominated first flare is by construction). A real fragmentation flare (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come from the model's deterministic cascade.
11 b bump 12.2817 29.544 1.6015e+14 stylized  Small fluctuation, 20% above the local trend; coincides with a yield (gen 3) at 29.5 km. The fine structure of this phase is set by the cascade rules, so its pattern is not predictive of a real event.
12 b bump 12.5038 28.435 1.4433e+14 stylized  Small fluctuation, 11% above the local trend; coincides with a split (gen 2) at 28.4 km. The fine structure of this phase is set by the cascade rules, so its pattern is not predictive of a real event.
13 - drag_overtakes_ablation 12.7800 27.195 7.3554e+13 stylized  Drag work now exceeds the kinetic energy carried off by ablated mass. The ratio ablation/drag is about Lambda v^2/(2 Q Cd), so this happens when the speed falls below ~14 km/s (from the model's heating law).
14 T tail 14.8140 21.670 2.6754e+11 low-confidence  Below 1e-3 of the peak the light is controlled by groups being retired when they slow below v_dark = 3.0 km/s and by the tau taper (2-4 km/s). Do not interpret structure below this level.
